{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/trinity-continuum-\u00e6on/1193208-psychic-fertility","id":1193208,"title":"Psychic Fertility","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum","Trinity Continuum: \u00c6on"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-03-08T11:06:36-08:00","id":1193208,"title":"Psychic Fertility","content":"I don't remember if this ever came up in 1e. Did Mesermeists, psiads, or Psions have any issues with fertility? Similarly in 2e are they inheritable traits? are Mersmerists/Psiads more likely to have psychic kids? are Psions more likely to have Latents?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T11:57:00-08:00","id":1193237,"title":"","content":"I don't know that it ever came up in 1e. Not that I distinctly remember.<br /> <br /> Nova stuff came up because it was a plot point in 1e (as discussed in another thread).<br /> <br /> There is some stuff in the Secrets Chapter that imply that Psionic potential is genetic, so I guess I'd say that barring a contrary statement from the devs that A&gt; Children of a Psion/Psiad/Mesmer are more likely to have Latency/Become Psychic than children of two non-psychics, and B&gt; Children of a Pair of Psychics (any flavor mix) are likely to have a higher base Latency/Psychic potential.<br /> <br /> Because that's how genetic things tend to work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/509-tiwaztyrsfist","name":"TiwazTyrsfist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar509_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T12:16:45-08:00","id":1193246,"title":"","content":"Considering how the Doyen seek to control and curb humanity's development of Psychic powers, it would be unusual for them to not consider how their gift of the Prometheus Chambers would affect the next generation.<br /> <br /> In all likelihood, the Chambers do not affect Psion fertility as the Doyen seek to use humanity against Aberrants and Novas... and to use them against other aliens that may pose a threat to the Doyen. As such, having a species that can maintain a large population is in the Doyen's best interests. However, they also want humanity to be dependent on the Doyen for their psychic advancement (as much as the Doyen allow that is), thus it is very likely that the Chambers do limit how humanity passes on the genes that control psychic development. Simply put, the child of a Psion will likely either be a neutral (no psychic power) or a Latent (psychic potential that can only be awoken through a Prometheus Chamber). Psions will likely never breed a Psiad (one who doesn't need a Chamber to awaken their power) because that could potentially free the species from Doyen control (and potentially allow the species to become more powerful than the Doyen; something that the Doyen want to avoid). Finally, it is unlikely that Psions will be able to breed other Psions, as the very definition of Psion is that their power is awoken through artificial means (usually the Prometheus Chambers).<br /> <br /> Currently it is unknown how fertile Psions are... and if their gifts (or potential to have such gifts) is passed on to the next generation... though the timeline does seem to be getting close to the point where the next generation should start coming into their power (where children born after 2104 are close to becoming adults)... and the first generation of Psions should have noticed if their children are gifted in any way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>There are three types of people in the world... those who can count and those who can't.<br /> I reject your reality and substitute my own!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2243-shadowstripe","name":"Shadowstripe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2243_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"344"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T13:22:13-08:00","id":1193283,"title":"","content":"My hous-ruling would be that Psi Latency is recessive. Two Psions are likely to have a Latent child viable to be dunked, a Psion and a non-Latent are not, though it\u2019s possible.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-03-08T14:38:00-08:00","id":1193312,"title":"","content":"I think that two Psions have a latent child as normal but that in time two Psions could also have a natural born Psiad child. This is very much &quot;human potential beats out Doyen tampering&quot; as well as a potential plot point for a campaign or saga.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}